---
import { site } from "../../lib/site";

/* SPEC §4c: the hardening readout. Marked illustrative in the body, at body
   size and colour, because these are not measurements from a named client.
   Hardening is the service we lead with, so this section also says plainly
   what the four weeks contain. */
const rows = [
  {
    metric: "p95 API response",
    before: "2400ms",
    after: "280ms",
    note: "Index audit, N+1 removal, connection pooling",
  },
  {
    metric: "Error rate",
    before: "3%",
    after: "0.4%",
    note: "Structured logging, then fixing what it showed",
  },
  {
    metric: "Integration tests",
    before: "0",
    after: "140",
    note: "Covering the path that takes the money",
  },
  {
    metric: "Deploys",
    before: "1/month",
    after: "9/week",
    note: "CI, migrations and a rollback that has been used",
  },
];

const weeks = [
  ["Week one: audit", "We read the codebase, the logs and the support inbox, reproduce the worst bugs, and agree with you the four numbers that define stable for your product."],
  ["Week two: fix what hurts users", "Crashes, failed payments, broken sign ups and slow pages come first, each one fixed with a test that stops it coming back."],
  ["Week three: tests, security and speed", "Automated tests across every critical flow, a security pass on authentication, data access and dependencies, and performance work on the slowest screens and endpoints."],
  ["Week four: release and handover", "CI/CD, monitoring and alerts in place, a production release you can roll back, and a runbook so your team or ours can keep it stable."],
];
---

<section class="v4-section" id="v4-hardening" aria-labelledby="v4-numbers-title">
  <div class="v4-container v4-split">
    <div class="v4-split__head">
      <p class="v4-eyebrow" data-v4-reveal>Product hardening from $1,999</p>
      <h2 class="v4-h2" id="v4-numbers-title" data-v4-reveal data-v4-delay="60">
        Your product is live and it keeps falling over. We fix that in four weeks.
      </h2>
      <p class="v4-body" data-v4-reveal data-v4-delay="120" style="margin-top: var(--v4-4)">
        Hardening is for software that already has users: built quickly, by an
        earlier developer or an AI coding tool, and now failing under real
        traffic. We fix the bugs, test every flow that matters, close the
        security gaps and make releases safe, so you can market the product
        with confidence.
      </p>
      <a
        class="v4-btn v4-btn--primary v4-magnet"
        data-v4-magnet
        href={site.booking}
        style="margin-top: var(--v4-6)"
      >
        Book a hardening call
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="v4-hardening">
      <ol class="v4-hardening__weeks" data-v4-group data-v4-step="90">
        {
          weeks.map(([title, body]) => (
            <li class="v4-hardening__week" data-v4-group-item>
              <h3 class="v4-h4">{title}</h3>
              <p class="v4-body" style="margin-top: var(--v4-2)">{body}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>

      <div>
        <h3 class="v4-h4">Four numbers have to move before we call it stable</h3>
        <p class="v4-body" style="margin-top: var(--v4-2); margin-bottom: var(--v4-5)">
          The figures below are illustrative. They show the shape of a typical
          four week engagement, not measurements from a named client. We agree
          your own four numbers in week one and report them every Friday.
        </p>

        <div class="v4-readout v4-card" data-v4-reveal>
          <div class="v4-readout__head v4-small">
            <span>Measure</span>
            <span>On arrival</span>
            <span>On handover</span>
          </div>

          {
            rows.map((row) => (
              <div class="v4-readout__row">
                <div class="v4-readout__metric">
                  <span>
                    <span class="v4-h5">{row.metric}</span>
                    <span class="v4-small v4-readout__note">{row.note}</span>
                  </span>
                </div>

                <div class="v4-readout__before v4-num">
                  <span data-v4-odometer={row.before}>{row.before}</span>
                </div>

                <div class="v4-readout__after v4-num">
                  <span data-v4-odometer={row.after} data-v4-hold="340">{row.after}</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
